bf331dd96d" :answer-field/choices ["q-337399/field-3/404c4e9a70878bb4f917f0c0c7110b4a7fa9b0dad236f95e4174179040937e25" "q-337399/field-3/2308e2b0bb3ea34a1e16133212a1e856ebfc62b81af4810e137463f6d22ea933" "q-337399/field-3/8413d9024f0049ca8259a6a31286b4d41e056a9d84919f890c2c8dbf331dd96d" "q-337399/field-3/acd10d12c8e6e434f56e9065aa7d642dd2f6866bdc9f37ec926f3adc1e7e2889"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337399" :question/id #uuid "a129942b-bc96-5e41-9abc-674cc7d1e75b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337399" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+2{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{-2x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{-2x})}^{′}+2(u{e}^{-2x}) & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-2u{e}^{-2x}+2u{e}^{-2x} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x}-\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}}+\\cancel{2u{e}^{-2x}} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{-2x} & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{-2x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{-2x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡3x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337399/field-1" "q-337399/field-2" "q-337399/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-1/59aba8fe2c8530b160c85567a2b9a38d332314fcb191a70e7c53192352669f6b" :answer/id #uuid "7f33d57a-9952-5af7-8cfe-d01e8664b1a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{15x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-1/0dfd7211371cc7d8403c054fcef962b61d8a8feaf3d34d77257754f397cd581b" :answer/id #uuid "79d6cf47-ac82-56c0-ab62-0d27a1561aea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-1/db4ed236e2a99bcf32827c539e941fd5a9aebd67b4dd13db98bf9f1d0e8f5b0a" :answer/id #uuid "eb8281e8-aa00-54b3-8522-43f12a25a0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-10x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-1/07c78099657bf21e505721b9