" :answer/id #uuid "b921c5fc-87f2-5c81-a9da-0a9103cb8997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "18e52400-1add-599a-9ab6-7a950dabc40b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337488/field-2/48ebb325525812d84be8e0c14f0aa66188310af1e9eaed985096f789d20492ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-337488/field-2/0855fcc906a7b7b01a6613b4fb2373595586ed243f8262eaa74ec8742c15c9eb" "q-337488/field-2/261b8ef6e8723a5a394c1097c9f18e472d66b4b97220048446e711330a0b0c95" "q-337488/field-2/f7e9c87fe4ecac4f8e31de701bf2a34ec5c5705a54baec247aaaa219d3e179ea" "q-337488/field-2/48ebb325525812d84be8e0c14f0aa66188310af1e9eaed985096f789d20492ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-3/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" :answer/id #uuid "e010c3b9-5c77-5f4b-8478-c5bfa85acd93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-3/9d3d0c12ff13c139e54d88e65e3903a204678f1298f7597091e06e6bf3a65fb3" :answer/id #uuid "756efd21-00ed-5ce4-834f-6a21fc5bb3ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-3/4e7280cd22327c2ba538c3921b3cdfa1cf343e100e973b659982e51f6ffac664" :answer/id #uuid "3a21437a-d2bf-5240-ae9c-328d5ccf766f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5x}-x{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-3/37177e90727d3601cb17824eef909face0cea78b2be953db134acaa24554c173" :answer/id #uuid "9bace0ea-9395-52aa-9d5f-8ba764b46e60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5x{e}^{5x}-{e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "85a9e798-3199-546c-b623-aefe1dcddb6f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-337488/field-3/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" :answer-field/choices ["q-337488/field-3/dd3378361514ba05f27e95e6befd7149234fafdfa6c0b12d143bc61c5e70723c" "q-337488/field-3/9d3d0c12ff13c139e54d88e65e3903a204678f1298f7597091e06e6bf3a65fb3" "q-337488/field-3/4e7280cd22327c2ba538c3921b3cdfa1cf343e100e973b659982e51f6ffac664" "q-337488/field-3/37177e90727d3601cb17824eef909face0cea78b2be953db134acaa24554c173"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337488" :question/id #uuid "5bf23900-2f3d-53c0-9448-69b2b01a2a2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337488" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{′}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{5x} & =10\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\ {u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x=\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}\n$$\n\nour equation for $u$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =10{e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡5x \\\\  & =10{e}^{-5x}(\\frac{{e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}}{2}) \\\\  & =5{e}^{-5x}({e}^{5x}+{e}^{-5x}) \\\\  & =5+5{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5+5{e}^{-10x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5+5{e}^{-10x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =5x-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-10x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =5x{e}^{5x}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-5x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337488/field-1" "q-337488/field-2" "q-337488/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337488"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337524/field-1/0dfd7211371cc7d8403c054fcef962b61d8a8feaf3d34d77257754f397cd581b" :answer/id #uuid "ad26962a-0a31-5443-9d04-672f1a357fea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337524/field-1/07c78099657bf21e505721b9fff971db5ba4f161a8aadba0cec9a268c3b7316c" :answer/id #uuid "03e16c96-e6e3-5d67-88a1-f1f496e8d91f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u(x){e}^{10x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337524/field-1/1c87915a6c57